def path(expl,bs,fs):
 return dict(explanation=expl,behavior_ids=bs,fact_ids=fs,source_ids=sorted({s for b in B if b['id'] in bs for s in b['source_ids']}))
formation=path('Apply creates a future and queues a command. Only the leader dispatches it, assigns term/index, calls StoreLogs and reports its own match. Per-peer workers send predecessor-qualified appends; followers reject stale terms or mismatching prefixes, truncate conflicting suffixes and store new entries before success. Ordinary and pipeline consumers use the corresponding request to report the last appended index; snapshot completion is an alternate support producer. commitment filters ServerIDs to latest voters, takes the majority match position and requires reaching the first index of this term. The main loop records commitment, processes the prefix and sends commit tuples to the FSM worker. runFSM completes command futures after callbacks. Later appends carry the commit bound to followers. Empty heartbeat success establishes contact without a replicated prefix. Store errors, retry/backoff, higher terms and shutdown take distinct paths.', ['B-api','B-dispatch','B-append','B-repl','B-commit','B-apply','B-snapshot'],['F-stored-support','F-append-success','F-leader-commit','F-application'])
context=path('Bootstrap persists initial term/configuration; NewRaft restores term, snapshot and configuration suffix before starting follower/FSM/snapshot workers. A voting follower with expired contact becomes candidate, optionally prevotes, then electSelf persists the new term and own vote and contacts latest voters. Vote handlers check leader, membership, term, prior vote and log freshness; majority grants on an attempt-local channel establish the local Leader role. Entry allocates new commitment/replication state and appends a no-op. Higher-term RPCs, higher-term data replies, loss of voter contact and committed removal can end leadership; cleanup stops replication and fails remaining inflight/verify futures. Transfer pauses writes, catches up a selected peer, sends TimeoutNow and still requires a real election. Verification is an additional public authority check based on asynchronous peer notifications, not the commit counter.', ['B-startup','B-elect','B-vote','B-authority-life','B-transfer','B-verify-register','B-heartbeat','B-verify-notify','B-verify-finish'],['F-vote','F-authority','F-peer-positive','F-verify-threshold'])
connection=path('Stored log/snapshot history survives leadership loss, but match tallies and response channels do not transfer into the next leader object. New authority uses log freshness in elections and a current-term startIndex/no-op to reconfirm advancement over old entries. Old replication workers retain old commitment/stepDown pointers; old election replies remain on old attempt channels. Remaining inflight calls fail on exit, whereas already queued committed FSM work may finish. Membership affects elections, commitment and leases via latest voter eligibility; configuration changes require stable prior membership and a current-term commit, and truncation can roll latest back. Snapshots bind an applied prefix to committed membership and reconstruct it at startup or resynchronization. Disaster recovery is explicitly exceptional and not interchangeable with normal Apply. VerifyLeader consumes response notifications through a separate boolean tally; its voter-eligibility and freshness meaning must be investigated rather than borrowed from commitment.', ['B-authority-life','B-membership','B-startup','B-snapshot','B-snapshot-save','B-user-restore','B-verify-register','B-verify-notify','B-verify-finish','B-apply'],['F-stored-support','F-leader-commit','F-authority','F-peer-positive','F-application'])
