question=dict(question='Can positive notifications from nonvoting replication peers satisfy a VerifyLeader future under fixed mixed membership without the voter support required for that public authority check?',importance='VerifyLeader is documented as preventing stale local FSM reads after leadership loss. If nonvoter support can substitute for an authority-confirming voter quorum, public success may mislead a read caller. This question does not yet establish a stale application read or an incorrect log decision.',source_ids=['S-api-verify','S-config-contract','S-verify-register','S-verify-vote','S-leader-loop','S-leader','S-repl','S-heartbeat','S-repl-update','S-snapshot-send','S-lease'],participants=['leader','voting followers','nonvoting followers','VerifyLeader caller'],objects=['verifyFuture','per-peer notify map','latest Configuration'],contexts=['fixed mixed voter/nonvoter membership','one actual leadership period','one VerifyLeader invocation through public completion'],event_paths=['bootstrap and actual election -> stable configuration -> VerifyLeader registration -> actual peer response production/delivery -> notifyAll -> vote -> leaderLoop future completion'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-repl','B-snapshot','B-heartbeat','B-verify-register','B-verify-notify','B-verify-finish'],fact_ids=['F-peer-positive'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-membership':'Defines actual voter/nonvoter roles and replication eligibility.','B-elect':'Establishes a real leader before the check.','B-authority-life':'Lease expiry, higher-term stepdown and cleanup are protective competing events.','B-commit':'Shows separately voter-filtered log commitment; its guarantees cannot be assumed for VerifyLeader.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['VerifyLeader returns errors on follower/candidate and on negative notification; leader exit fails pending verification.','Voter-only lease checks can end authority even if nonvoters respond.','Normal commitment explicitly excludes nonvoter matches; no incorrect log commitment follows from this registration asymmetry alone.','The API does not literally state a voter-quorum formula; its authority/read purpose needs a justified requirement derivation.'],unknowns=['Applicable requirement: derive the necessary support condition for this authority API without turning implementation asymmetry into its own oracle.','Actual producer: execute actual nonvoter reply production and its consumption, not a synthetic vote(bool).','Initial prefix: observe real election and settled mixed membership with public configuration and committed operation.','Same execution: exclude old voter replies as contributors, retain negative replies/lease/stepdown workers, and correlate the checked future interval.','Observed endpoint: measure the same public future result; stale FSM read and newer-leader application are separate unobserved consequences.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Source trace found verifyLeader registers every replState entry, while quorumSize counts voters; vote receives no peer identity/suffrage. This concrete producer-consumer relation makes eligibility the best next discriminator. A fixed configuration bounds configuration-transition ambiguity.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')
